From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: erosqcfw <erosqcfw@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 20:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH BlueZ] a2dp: guard NULL setup->sep/session in auto_config()

bluetoothd SIGSEGVs when connecting some A2DP sinks (reproduced with a UE
MEGABOOM). Two racing-teardown variants, both fixed here:

1. read @0x14 (struct a2dp_sep .stream): select_cb() nulls setup->sep via
   queue_pop_head(setup->eps) when no valid config can be selected; a racing
   async SetConfiguration reply then reaches auto_config() via
   endpoint_setconf_cb() with setup->sep already NULL.

2. read @0x450 (struct avdtp .in_cmd.transaction): remove_channel() finalizes
   the pending setup with -ENOTCONN (setup->err set) and NULLs setup->session
   when the A2DP channel drops mid-config; a pending g_idle_add(auto_config)
   then passes the sep guard, takes the err!=NULL -> goto done path (skipping
   the avdtp_get_device(setup->session) deref) and calls
   setup->setconf_cb(setup->session=NULL, ...) -> avdtp setconf_cb()
   dereferences session->in_cmd.transaction -> crash.

Either way bluetoothd crash-loops (respawned by the UI's org.bluez name
watch), pinning CPU + churning RAM. Treat a NULL sep OR session like the
existing "configuration aborted" case (stream==NULL): abort cleanly.
setup->session is already assumed nullable elsewhere (a2dp_setup_get_device
null-checks it).

The abort path must also drop auto_config()'s setup reference: both callers
hand it one ref that only the setup_unref() at the tail of the normal path
releases (endpoint_setconf_ind's a2dp_setup_get() ref on the
g_idle_add(auto_config) path; the extra setup_ref() passed through
endpoint->set_configuration() on the endpoint_setconf_cb() path -- that
callback's own unref only balances the a2dp_setup_get() ref). Without the
unref the aborted setup stays in the module-global setups list forever.
Upstream's narrower stream==NULL early return has the same latent leak; the
widened guard makes it reachable in practice, so release the ref here.


Rebased onto 5.86: auto_config() now calls avdtp_get_device(session) and
reads setup->sep->type BEFORE any abort check, and aborts on a missing
stream via queue_find(sep->streams) instead of sep->stream. So the guard
moves to the top (sep/session only), and the two new upstream early
returns (no btd service, stream not found) get the same setup_unref() --
both callers still hand auto_config() one ref.

Signed-off-by: erosqcfw <erosqcfw@gmail.com>
---
 profiles/audio/a2dp.c

diff --git a/profiles/audio/a2dp.c b/profiles/audio/a2dp.c
--- a/profiles/audio/a2dp.c
+++ b/profiles/audio/a2dp.c
@@ -718,6 +718,19 @@
 	struct btd_service *service;
 	struct a2dp_stream *stream;
 
+	/* setup->sep can be NULL: the per-session setup is shared, and
+	 * select_cb() nulls it via queue_pop_head(setup->eps) when no valid
+	 * config can be selected. setup->session can be NULL too:
+	 * remove_channel() NULLs it (with setup->err set) when the channel
+	 * drops mid-config, and a pending g_idle_add(auto_config) then reaches
+	 * setconf_cb() with a NULL session -> crash. Seen connecting to some
+	 * A2DP sinks (e.g. UE MEGABOOM). Abort cleanly, releasing the ref the
+	 * tail of the normal path would have dropped. */
+	if (setup->sep == NULL || setup->session == NULL) {
+		setup_unref(setup);
+		return FALSE;
+	}
+
 	dev = avdtp_get_device(setup->session);
 
 	if (setup->sep->type == AVDTP_SEP_TYPE_SOURCE)
@@ -727,13 +740,16 @@
 
 	if (service == NULL) {
 		error("Unable to find btd service");
+		setup_unref(setup);
 		return FALSE;
 	}
 
 	/* Check if configuration was aborted */
 	stream = queue_find(setup->sep->streams, match_stream, setup->stream);
-	if (!stream)
+	if (!stream) {
+		setup_unref(setup);
 		return FALSE;
+	}
 
 	if (setup->err != NULL)
 		goto done;
